        <mxCell id="note_rules" value="&lt;b&gt;Reading it&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Every namespace inside the fenced frame starts from deny-all-ingress (Kyverno generates it for tier=app namespaces; identity carries a committed copy), so an arrow is the only way in. Not drawn, but allowed: the ten service namespaces reach identity :8080 for JWKS; pods inside product reach each other on :5432 / :6432 / :8000 and inside platform on :5432 / :8000; envoy-gateway and the service mesh reach the services on :8080 / :9090 (§ 3)." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="600" width="1060" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note_limits" value="&lt;b&gt;Not fenced (yet)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No egress rules exist anywhere, so DNS and outbound traffic are open. mTLS on gRPC :9090 and a ClickHouse policy for :9000 / :8123 are planned follow-ups, not deployed." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="682" width="1060" height="40" as="geometry" />
